<task id="225b" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Converge Model 1 onto the dedicated code path — H2b / H12c shared-platform branches out, tenancy × profile pairing (G6), secret-free default (G21), Bing + LlamaParse keys out (D18), `Model1SharedDagParityTests` rename (G13)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T225b (gaps G6, G13, G21; owner decisions D12-era D-12 + D18)</phase>
    <gate>startable — T225a ✅ (b9fd48bbe); owner decisions D16–D19 recorded (6240f41d8)</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs handlers, options, validation and tests across H2b, H12c, H4, the Api edge and the Worker; edits Bicep + the canonical secret catalog; credential-lifecycle constraints apply (G21).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting convergence touching 5 handlers/options sets, the Api edge, the secret catalog generator and Bicep (high blast radius), plus a credential-lifecycle default (G21) bound by BINDING KV rules.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ (provision-environment skill prose) — main-session-only; file overlap with T249 (customer.json, controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep) and T248 (Worker Bicep module)</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, l2-controlplane, provisioning-handler, bicep, testing, model1-dedicated, secret-catalog</tags>
    <deps>225a</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make a Model 1 run use the same per-stamp resources as the dedicated code path: retire the H2b and H12c branches that
    point Model 1 at a shared platform AI Search / OpenAI, pair Model 1 with the Spaarke-hosted dedicated profile at
    intake, make new stamps secret-free by default, and remove the dead Bing / LlamaParse vendor keys from the customer
    secret catalog. Leave ArmDeploymentRunner's Model 1 arm failing closed — T228 flips it together with per-customer
    subscriptions.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer on the L2 provisioning control plane (.NET 10, Azure SDK, Bicep). Follow ADRs strictly;
    apply the KV credential-lifecycle rules in .claude/constraints/provisioning.md literally.
  </role>

  <goal>
    No control-plane code path, option, Bicep setting or seed script points a Model 1 run at a shared platform service;
    `POST /api/runs` pairs `Model1` ↔ `spaarke-hosted-model2` and `Model2` ↔ `customer-owned-model2` only; H4 omits
    `Dataverse-ClientSecret` + `BFF-API-ClientSecret` on a new stamp by default and their `PinnedManifestGaps` pins are
    gone; the customer secret catalog has no `BingSearch-ApiKey` / `LlamaParse-ApiKey`; no file or class is named
    `Model1Shared*`. Model 1 runs still fail closed at H2a (T228).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      D-12 (owner 2026-09-30) redefined Model 1 as a per-customer dedicated stamp. T225a deleted the shared-tier Bicep and
      made ArmDeploymentRunner fail closed for Model 1. What is left of the shared tier is control-plane code: H2b creates
      Model 1 indexes on `AiSearchIndexOptions.SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint` with a tenant-filter query template
      (`IAiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisioner`); H12c points Model 1 runtime references at
      `RuntimeReferencesOptions.SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` (seeded by `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` as
      `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint`, emitted by the Worker Bicep as `RuntimeReferences__SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint`). The intake
      validator still pairs Model 1 with the retired trial profile `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial`, although H3's
      `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner` and INCOMING §5 Item 3 already treat `spaarke-hosted-model2` as the Spaarke-hosted
      dedicated (= Model 1) profile (G6). New stamps run MI-FIC (ADR-028 A4, E-3 closed) but
      `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.RequireSecretFreeIdentity` defaults false and is set nowhere, so H4 would serve
      `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (G21). Owner D18 (2026-10-02): Bing + LlamaParse keys leave customer stamps — Bing Search v7
      was retired 2025-08-11, LlamaParse has no production caller, and no value exists in any vault.
    </background>
