  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-027 (amended) + T225a adr-check F2">
      Do NOT change `ArmDeploymentRunner`'s Model 1 arm — it keeps failing closed (`arm-template-unavailable`) until T228
      brings per-customer subscriptions; T228 flips it. Do not remove the ISH-02 Model 1 subscription exemption (T228).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/provisioning.md § KV credential lifecycle (BINDING)">
      No live Key Vault write, delete or purge in this task. Never create, seed or restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either
      casing) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in a secret-free environment. In `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` change ONLY the
      `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint` entry and the header/example count drift — do not touch the `Dataverse-ClientSecret`,
      `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `Sidecar-Shared-Secret`, `Exchange-Connect-Cert` or `Redis-ConnectionString` entries.
      `SecretFreeIdentityRollback` semantics stay as they are.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D18 (2026-10-02)">
      Remove `BingSearch-ApiKey` and `LlamaParse-ApiKey` from `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` and
      regenerate every generated output with the generator (never hand-edit generated files). If, after the removal, no
      manifest entry uses `value_source: from-platform-vault`, remove that value source end to end: the resolver branch,
      the H4 writer's vendor-key pre-write check, `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.PlatformVaultName` + its boot validation,
      the manifest schema enum value, and the Worker Bicep `vendorKeysKeyVaultName` param + its
      `KvSecretsPopulationOptions__PlatformVaultName` setting (a required boot option nothing reads is a failure mode).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="plan G6 + INCOMING §5 Item 3">
      Pairing after this task: `Model1` ↔ `spaarke-hosted-model2`; `Model2` ↔ `customer-owned-model2`. Every other pair,
      including any pair using `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial`, is refused with the existing invalid-pair error code. Do NOT
      rename the profile vocabulary (out of scope — record a one-line follow-up for T235 if you think it should be).
      Record the change as an extension of the T245a ADR-020 row in spec.md ADR Tensions (same callers, same reasoning).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 / project scope">
      No change to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api` (the BFF's dead Bing v7 code is on the BFF follow-up list).
      `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` untouched (T228). `H0Options.RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated` /
      `isModel2Dedicated` are T229 — do not rename them here.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="Sub-agent write boundary">
      `.claude/**` edits (provision-environment skill prose, CHANGELOG, constraints/patterns if they name a removed option)
      are made by the main session.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint`, the tenant-filter template provisioner or `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` has a consumer that is not the Model 1 branch → STOP and report before deleting it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Making secret-free the default would change the behaviour of a run against an existing live environment (e.g. the prong-3 `spaarkedev1` exception, sunset 2026-11-23) → STOP; do not work around it with a new flag.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing the `from-platform-vault` value source would require a change outside the control plane, the catalog generator, its schema and the Worker Bicep (e.g. the BFF) → STOP; keep the mechanism, make `PlatformVaultName` optional, and record why.</trigger>
    <trigger>The registry (`sprk_dataverseenvironment`) or any stored artifact carries profile values the new pairing would orphan → STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Confirm the branch is 0 behind origin/master (re-merge if not). `git grep -n` for `SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint`, `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint`, `TenantFilterTemplate`, `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial`, `Model1Shared`, `BingSearch`, `LlamaParse`, `from-platform-vault`, `PlatformVaultName`, `vendorKeysKeyVaultName` → categorized hit list in the POML notes.</step>
    <step order="1">H2b: route `TenancyModel.Model1` to the dedicated branch; delete `HandleModel1BranchAsync`, the shared endpoint option, the tenant-filter template provisioner (interface, implementation, DI, rejection codes) and their Worker/Bicep settings. Update H2b tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H12c: same for the OpenAI endpoint; remove `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` from options, module, rejection codes, Worker Program, Bicep (module + platform-controlplane + recompiled JSON + dev bicepparam) and the `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint` entry of `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` (fix its "6 secrets" / "seed all 5" count drift). Update H12c tests.</step>
    <step order="3">G6: validator pairing in `RunsEndpoints` + `KnownProfiles`; `intake.schema.json` allOf; RunsEndpointsTests + every fixture that pairs Model1 with the trial profile; spec.md ADR-020 row extension; skill Step 1c / 1e prose (main session).</step>
    <step order="4">G21: secret-free by default for new stamps — `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.RequireSecretFreeIdentity` true by default AND set explicitly in the Worker Bicep; remove the `Dataverse-ClientSecret` / `BFF-API-ClientSecret` pins from `RunContextContractTests.PinnedManifestGaps`. Check the H2a `requireSecretFreeIdentity` intake key and `customer.bicep` param: if nothing consumes the Bicep param, remove both (and the ArmDeploymentRunner payload entry); if something does, default it true. Record the evidence.</step>
    <step order="5">D18: manifest removal + regenerate (generator `-Verify` clean); the `from-platform-vault` removal per the constraint; recompile `customer.json` / `platform-controlplane.json` if their inputs changed (`az bicep build --outfile`, never `--stdout`).</step>
    <step order="6">G13: rename `Model1SharedDagParityTests.cs` (file + class) to a name that states what it pins (e.g. `TenancyModelDagParityTests`).</step>
    <step order="7">Docs: inventory, deployment guide, prerequisites guide / `prereqs.yaml` (+ `validate.ps1`), gap note — remove the shared-endpoint and vendor-key rows; `.claude` constraints/patterns that name a removed option (main session) + CHANGELOG.</step>
    <step order="8">Verify: ControlPlane Api/Worker/Tests/LoadTests build 0 warnings 0 errors; ControlPlane.Tests — no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; prereqs `validate.ps1` OK; catalog `-Verify` OK; repeat the Step 0 grep → only historical records remain (list them).</step>
    <step order="9">Step 9.5 quality gates (code-review + adr-check). Close: POML notes, TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`, plan §4 G6/G13/G21 + §7 T225b, current-task.md; `scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`. Commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the ControlPlane solution projects and ArchTests</tool>
    <tool name="az">`az bicep build --outfile` only</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Catalog generator, prereqs validate.ps1, bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1, check-task-status-drift.ps1</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">H2b / H12c / RunsEndpoints / KvSecretsPopulation / Worker Program changes; deleted tenant-filter template provisioner</output>
    <output type="config">manifest.yaml + regenerated outputs; intake.schema.json; Worker + platform-controlplane Bicep (+ JSON); Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">Updated H2b, H12c, RunsEndpoints, H4, RunContextContract tests; renamed DAG parity test</output>
    <output type="docs">inventory, deployment guide, prerequisites, gap note, spec ADR-020 row, plan §4/§7, skill prose, CHANGELOG</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Model 1 run, H2b creates indexes on the AI Search endpoint H2a produced, through the same code path as Model 2; given that output is absent, it fails with the same rejection code Model 2 uses. No `HandleModel1BranchAsync`, `SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint` or tenant-filter template provisioner remains in code, DI, Worker config or Bicep.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Model 1 run, H12c's OpenAI runtime reference is the stamp's own endpoint; no `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` remains in code, Worker config, Bicep (incl. compiled JSON) or `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/runs` accepts `Model1`+`spaarke-hosted-model2` and `Model2`+`customer-owned-model2`; it refuses `Model1`+`spaarke-hosted-model1-trial`, `Model1`+`customer-owned-model2` and `Model2`+`spaarke-hosted-model2` with the existing invalid-pair code; `intake.schema.json` agrees (schema/endpoint parity test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With default options, H4 writes neither `Dataverse-ClientSecret` nor `BFF-API-ClientSecret`; the Worker Bicep sets `KvSecretsPopulationOptions__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`; `PinnedManifestGaps` contains only the T246 and T227 pins; existing rollback tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The canonical secret catalog has no `BingSearch-ApiKey` or `LlamaParse-ApiKey`; generated files match the generator (`-Verify` OK); either the `from-platform-vault` mechanism and `PlatformVaultName` are gone end to end, or (escalation 3) the option is optional and the reason is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file or type name in src/ contains `Model1Shared`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ArmDeploymentRunner`'s Model 1 arm still throws (its T2 test unchanged); `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` and `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api` unchanged; no live Key Vault operation performed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane projects build 0/0; ControlPlane.Tests has no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; prereqs `validate.ps1` OK.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the changed contracts and the negative cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the POML notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-02 from plan §7 T225b + owner D18. Scope change vs the plan row: the ArmDeploymentRunner Model 1 → `customer`
    flip moved to T228 (flipping it before per-customer subscriptions exist would deploy a full stamp into a shared
    subscription — T225a adr-check F2 / ADR-027).
  </notes>

